{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339126 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23b28d03-cd57-5d78-8671-e5c1d46ed665" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467938} {:answer/id #uuid "8ed66caf-fe28-584a-83bf-1f36896c365e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467939}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467938} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cd09d61-c1f0-556d-8c4e-0dd624a70cf5" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468690} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b617e07-2740-58b3-b6a5-d9472e257ceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467940} {:answer/id #uuid "b4308405-a8a5-56c9-af60-06c16d1d14d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467941}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467941} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ee97b22-001a-5361-9e3b-138ef357939a" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468691} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94af9650-c777-5740-9917-82f863d1fd15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467942} {:answer/id #uuid "3369f3e3-6e3d-5e75-b2a8-d84fac360cef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467943}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186467943} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d389fe9-b790-5945-910d-6661d44a7238" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9ddf8ccb-f483-5bbe-8662-ef5250ea89a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-72489" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry ${c}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are **not** in row echelon form."}
